Which rectangle meets all three conditions?

Its shorter side is less than $5\text{ cm}$, its area is more than $30\text{ cm}^2$, and its perimeter is $26\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},x=4mm,y=4mm]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (9,4);
\path (4.5,4) node[above] {A} (4.5,0) node[below] {$9\mathrm{\ cm}$} (9,2) node[right] {$4\mathrm{\ cm}$};
\draw (14,0) rectangle (8+14,5);
\path (18,5) node[above] {B} (18,0) node[below] {$8\mathrm{\ cm}$} (22,2.5) node[right] {$5\mathrm{\ cm}$};
\draw (0,-9) rectangle (10,-6);
\path (5,-6) node[above] {C} (5,-9) node[below] {$10\mathrm{\ cm}$} (10,-7.5) node[right] {$3\mathrm{\ cm}$};
\draw (14,-9) rectangle (24,-5);
\path (19,-5) node[above] {D} (19,-9) node[below] {$10\mathrm{\ cm}$} (24,-7) node[right] {$4\mathrm{\ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
